      "tip": "**আপনি has two command forms, both polite.**\n\n- **Everyday Bangladesh:** the আপনি present form, as in **দেন**, **যান**, **থামেন**: **বসেন** 'sit', **বলেন** 'say'.\n- **Standard (signs, offices, Kolkata):** take the আমি form, drop -ই, add **-উন**: বসি → **বসুন**, বলি → **বলুন**, শুনি → **শুনুন**, আসি → **আসুন**. Like **দিন**, 'take' is **নিন**.\n\n**ভিতরে আসুন, বসুন** 'Come in, have a seat' is what a host says. **শুনুন** 'listen' is also how you politely say 'Excuse me' to a stranger.\n\n**দয়া করে** 'please' is formal or pleading; the polite verb already does most of the work.",
